# Paintdex environment variables
#
# User accounts (optional) are powered by Supabase, called directly from the
# browser. Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and set both
# values from your Supabase project (Project Settings → API). In production,
# set the same two variables in the Vercel project (Production, Preview and
# Development environments).
#
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_* and are inlined into the client bundle at build time.
# This is expected and safe: the anon key is a public, publishable key —
# access is enforced by Row-Level Security policies (see supabase/schema.sql),
# not by keeping the key secret.
#
# If these are unset, the site still runs fully — accounts/sign-in features are
# simply hidden and the visualiser falls back to localStorage-only, as before.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase's dashboard now labels this the "publishable" key (formerly "anon").
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google OAuth client ID for the "Sign in with Google" button (Google Identity
# Services ID-token flow). Public by design. Create it in Google Cloud →
# Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application) and add your site origins
# (http://localhost:3000, https://paintdex.app) to "Authorized JavaScript
# origins". Add this same Client ID to Supabase → Auth → Providers → Google →
# "Client IDs". If unset, sign-in falls back to Supabase's redirect flow, which
# shows the supabase.co domain on Google's consent screen.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
